WEBVTT

00:27.600 --> 00:30.570
Congratulations!

00:41.110 --> 00:44.550
Welcome to the 7G Network Launch Ceremony!

00:44.550 --> 00:48.170
You're none other than the 
77,777th person here!

00:44.560 --> 00:47.810
<b>Congrats on Being 77,777th</b>

00:48.170 --> 00:49.070
Tell us your name!

00:49.070 --> 00:49.910
Huh?

00:49.910 --> 00:51.230
A-Ah...

00:52.880 --> 00:54.580
Nakatomi Yoka.

00:54.580 --> 00:56.450
Welcome, Yoka-san!

00:56.450 --> 01:01.020
I'm the head of the Spread 7G Worldwide 
Committee, Poison Pontaro!

01:01.020 --> 01:06.220
Yoka-san, what do you expect from 7G, 
which will connect the world at record speed?

01:08.670 --> 01:09.570
What do I expect?

01:09.570 --> 01:10.620
Yes!

01:10.620 --> 01:13.240
Instant communication and contact 
with anyone, anywhere!

01:13.240 --> 01:15.800
That's the magic of the new 
technology that is 7G!

01:15.800 --> 01:17.690
We couldn't catch up at all for 5G!

01:17.690 --> 01:19.640
Totally late to the game with 6G!

01:19.640 --> 01:22.510
But now, we'll reclaim our 
national honor with 7G!

01:22.510 --> 01:24.980
There were those who opposed us!

01:24.980 --> 01:26.140
Smear campaigns, even!

01:26.140 --> 01:29.730
But we didn't back down in the face 
of their baseless fake news!

01:29.730 --> 01:33.900
All the world's leading technologies, 
crammed, stuffed, and hammered into 7G!

01:33.900 --> 01:37.010
Tap directly into the thoughts in your brain 
for an omni-device approach!

01:37.010 --> 01:39.620
Thoughts, instantly broadcast! 
Visions, instantly made real!

01:39.620 --> 01:42.690
Harness the very power of God, only with...

01:42.690 --> 01:44.310
7G!

01:43.320 --> 01:45.620
Um, can I leave—

01:46.580 --> 01:47.980
Without further ado...

01:47.980 --> 01:49.900
Let us all be witnesses!

01:49.900 --> 01:51.680
For this historic moment 
paving the way to tomorrow!

01:52.250 --> 01:53.270
Five!

01:53.790 --> 01:54.580
Four!

01:55.120 --> 01:56.090
Three!

01:56.690 --> 01:57.600
Two!

01:58.260 --> 01:59.330
One!

01:59.770 --> 02:01.620
Open the...

02:01.620 --> 02:04.730
Future!

02:06.170 --> 02:09.070
Open the future!

02:36.600 --> 02:40.400
What the hell?!

02:57.320 --> 03:01.070
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

04:12.520 --> 04:17.190
About 2 Years Later

04:16.340 --> 04:17.180
Shizuru.

04:17.190 --> 04:21.570
<b>Agano Station</b>

04:17.730 --> 04:21.570
Episode 1        I'll Be Going Now

04:18.880 --> 04:21.570
Are you even thinking about your future?

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b>Career Path Survey{top line}</b>

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Year 2 - Shizuru Chikura

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>1st Pref.

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>2nd Pref.

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>3rd Pref.

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>4th Pref.

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Higher Ed.
Employment
<u><b>Other</b></u>

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Higher Ed.
Employment
<u><b>Other</b></u>

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Higher Ed.
Employment
<u><b>Other</b></u>

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Higher Ed.
Employment
<u><b>Other</b></u>

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Look for her

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Look for her

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Look for her

04:21.570 --> 04:25.530
<b></b>Look for her

04:22.090 --> 04:25.530
Do you really think I'd accept 
these ridiculous answers?

04:25.530 --> 04:28.340
Besides, it's already been two years—

04:29.770 --> 04:31.000
Sorry.

04:31.600 --> 04:35.050
<i>This is an Agano Station District broadcast.</i>

04:35.050 --> 04:40.130
<i>The Black Leopard caravan will be 
arriving soon at Agano-juku-mae.</i>

04:40.590 --> 04:47.020
<i>Please gather if you have packages to send 
or receive or wish to make any purchases.</i>

04:49.730 --> 04:50.660
Oh?

04:50.660 --> 04:52.660
If it isn't Kazuyo-san and Granny Oito.

04:52.660 --> 04:55.220
Why, we ran into each other by the bridge.

04:55.220 --> 04:59.410
I thought you two got into a fight 
over some burlap sacks.

04:59.410 --> 05:01.700
That's all behind us now.

05:01.700 --> 05:04.460
And have you made up with 
Kikko-chan yet, Masaharu?

05:04.460 --> 05:06.440
Well, not exactly.

05:06.440 --> 05:08.950
Moaned about her cooking again, I'm sure.

05:08.950 --> 05:11.030
Don't complain when she's the one making it.

05:11.030 --> 05:14.980
You say that, but I'm a bear, 
and she's a muntjac.

05:14.980 --> 05:16.700
Our tastes are night and day now.

05:16.700 --> 05:17.880
Tastes?

05:17.880 --> 05:19.190
How small-minded.

05:19.190 --> 05:20.540
Am not!

05:20.540 --> 05:22.800
In the end, it's just food.

05:22.800 --> 05:23.930
That's right.

05:23.930 --> 05:25.990
Agano got off easy with animals.

05:25.990 --> 05:29.200
Why, I hear there are places 
where everyone turned into trees.

05:29.200 --> 05:29.740
Trees?

05:29.740 --> 05:31.220
The ones covering the mountains!

05:31.220 --> 05:33.320
We're lucky to be animals who can move!

05:33.320 --> 05:34.620
You think?

05:34.620 --> 05:36.720
As a bear, I get hungry so quickly.

05:36.720 --> 05:39.700
If only <i>you</i> had turned 
into a tree, Masaharu.

05:39.700 --> 05:41.840
Or a rock, or a mushroom, 
or a horsehair worm.

05:41.840 --> 05:42.740
Wow, that's harsh.

05:42.740 --> 05:45.390
Once you get used to it, 
life as an animal isn't so bad.

05:45.390 --> 05:47.170
I mean, sure.

05:47.170 --> 05:49.100
I've spent two years as a bear.

05:49.100 --> 05:50.660
I'm used to it by now.

05:50.660 --> 05:51.920
That's right.

05:51.920 --> 05:55.240
Atsushi just turned into an aye-aye, 
and he still hasn't gotten over it.

05:55.530 --> 05:58.360
That was Atsushi I saw 
roaming around at night?

05:58.360 --> 06:00.640
He's that age already, huh?

06:01.060 --> 06:04.950
He said he'd have left Agano 
if he'd known this would happen.

06:04.950 --> 06:08.630
He can leave all he wants, but Agano folk 
will always turn into birds or mammals.

06:08.630 --> 06:09.350
Oh, right.

06:09.350 --> 06:12.380
Even if you leave, you're still stuck 
turning into an animal, huh?

06:12.380 --> 06:13.260
That reminds me.

06:13.260 --> 06:15.760
Remember the kid who went missing 
before the 7G incident?

06:15.760 --> 06:18.010
I wonder what she's up to now.

06:18.010 --> 06:20.730
I think that Chikura girl 
is still looking for her.

06:20.730 --> 06:22.300
It'd be one thing if she were in Agano,

06:22.300 --> 06:26.020
but what if she turned into an animal 
in an unfamiliar place, all alone?

06:26.020 --> 06:27.660
What else can you do but adapt?

06:27.930 --> 06:28.940
Ugh.

06:28.940 --> 06:32.420
At least we don't have to pay for 
health insurance or pensions anymore.

06:32.750 --> 06:35.370
It's not like there are even any clinics left,

06:35.370 --> 06:38.050
and all that fussy bureaucracy's 
a thing of the past now.

06:38.050 --> 06:39.960
If you go all the way out to Inariyama Park,

06:39.960 --> 06:42.280
you can find a really good doctor in the area.

06:42.280 --> 06:44.100
Or so I hear, anyway.

06:44.100 --> 06:45.700
Not happening!

06:45.700 --> 06:48.670
Who knows how many years 
you'd waste trying to get out there.

06:48.670 --> 06:51.180
Or whether you can even make it there alive.

06:51.420 --> 06:54.340
Also, you don't even know whether 
they're a human doctor or not.

06:54.340 --> 06:56.520
A human doctor, you say?

06:56.520 --> 06:58.130
They might be a doctor who treats humans.

06:58.130 --> 06:59.800
Or a doctor who's still a human.

07:00.150 --> 07:03.870
Oh, you mean they might treat humans 
but not be human anymore?

07:03.870 --> 07:07.020
Or they can't treat humans, 
but they happen to be in human form?

07:07.020 --> 07:10.100
That skilled doctor 
in Inariyama Park, that is.

07:10.100 --> 07:12.310
Is that like that "poop that 
tastes like curry" thing?

07:12.310 --> 07:13.910
That's so gross, Akira.

07:13.910 --> 07:14.810
Huh?

07:14.810 --> 07:16.600
I'm just asking a metaphysical question here.

07:16.600 --> 07:17.650
The heck's that mean?

07:17.960 --> 07:19.090
You girls.

07:19.090 --> 07:22.190
Are you going on about curry and 
whatnot because you're hungry?

07:22.190 --> 07:25.150
If you don't mind crickets, 
I'm happy to share some of mine.

07:25.150 --> 07:26.520
No, thank you!

07:26.520 --> 07:28.380
There's nothing wrong with 
eating bugs nowadays.

07:28.380 --> 07:29.910
No way! They're not cute!

07:29.910 --> 07:31.420
I heard that they're nutritious.

07:31.420 --> 07:33.380
Nutrition's not the issue!

07:33.380 --> 07:36.290
Since the incident, we get a huge 
rice harvest six times a year,

07:36.290 --> 07:38.350
not to mention bitter melon, 
so I get plenty of calories.

07:38.350 --> 07:40.970
What I really need 
is cuteness and adventure!

07:40.970 --> 07:43.050
Ugh, here comes the rampant escapism.

07:43.050 --> 07:45.450
Or is it just excessive optimism? 
Head in the clouds?

07:45.450 --> 07:48.760
I know exactly what you're 
trying to say, Akira.

07:48.760 --> 07:50.060
You're making fun of me, aren't you?

07:50.060 --> 07:51.370
Bingo!

07:51.370 --> 07:52.860
You make me so mad!

07:52.860 --> 07:53.900
Learn more words.

07:55.810 --> 07:58.040
Don't resort to fighting, no matter what!

07:58.040 --> 07:59.640
Akira started it!

07:58.880 --> 08:00.540
No! Bad!

08:01.490 --> 08:03.050
You got yelled at!

08:03.050 --> 08:05.500
You got yelled at by Nadeko-chan!

08:04.770 --> 08:06.860
That goes for you too, Akira-chan!

08:07.710 --> 08:08.570
Okay.

08:08.570 --> 08:09.360
There.

08:09.360 --> 08:11.090
Good girl, Akira-chan.

08:11.090 --> 08:12.910
You're a good girl too, Reimi-chan.

08:12.910 --> 08:14.500
They sure are late.

08:14.500 --> 08:15.810
Hey, Nadeko-chan.

08:15.810 --> 08:18.070
Don't you think the Black Leopard 
caravan is awfully late?

08:18.070 --> 08:20.620
I'll say. We've been waiting all this time.

08:20.220 --> 08:21.850
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

08:20.220 --> 08:21.850
<b>FROM:
Black Leopard Delivery
SUB: Delivery Notice
Thank you for your
continued business.
We will arrive shortly</b>

08:20.620 --> 08:22.730
I received a message on my PHS,

08:22.730 --> 08:24.780
which should mean they're pretty close.

08:24.780 --> 08:27.580
What if everyone from Black 
Leopard got wiped out?

08:27.580 --> 08:28.860
That'd be bad!

08:28.860 --> 08:30.860
My mook is supposed to arrive today.

08:30.860 --> 08:32.450
Shizuru-chan's not here, either.

08:32.820 --> 08:34.400
You're right. That's new.

08:34.400 --> 08:37.490
Doesn't she have her career consultation 
with Iguchi-sensei today?

08:37.490 --> 08:39.480
Oh, career stuff, huh?

08:39.480 --> 08:41.650
Not that there's any point to discussing it.

08:41.650 --> 08:43.920
What a sad thing to say.

08:43.920 --> 08:44.700
Come now.

08:44.700 --> 08:46.770
There's nothing sad about it.

08:46.770 --> 08:47.810
Just cold, hard facts.

08:47.810 --> 08:50.330
Oh? Is that Zenjiro-san I spot?

08:50.330 --> 08:52.060
A scenic hallmark of Agano.

08:52.060 --> 08:54.300
He used to be so tall and handsome.

08:54.300 --> 08:56.720
But when he came back 
to Agano two years ago,

08:56.720 --> 08:59.140
he'd become unable to say anything 
other than "choo-choo."

08:59.560 --> 09:03.850
The weird thing about Zenjiro-san 
is that he managed to stay human.

09:03.850 --> 09:06.670
Everyone else in Agano turns into an animal

09:06.670 --> 09:09.460
when they turn 21 years 
and three months old.

09:09.460 --> 09:10.740
Now that you mention it...

09:10.740 --> 09:11.440
That's right.

09:11.970 --> 09:16.650
We'll eventually turn into 
some sort of animal, too.

09:16.650 --> 09:17.950
And you can't pick which one.

09:18.240 --> 09:19.590
Sure are late...

09:19.590 --> 09:20.600
There you go again.

09:20.600 --> 09:21.630
Can you blame me?

09:21.630 --> 09:24.390
I might be able to eat meat 
for the first time in so long!

09:24.390 --> 09:27.010
Do you prefer eating meat, then?

09:27.010 --> 09:29.220
Over rice, sweet potatoes, and bitter melon?

09:29.220 --> 09:30.900
Well, duh!

09:30.900 --> 09:32.260
Meat is so good.

09:32.260 --> 09:33.370
I'd love me some meat.

09:33.370 --> 09:36.990
A steak, tender and bloody rare...

09:36.990 --> 09:38.730
No, super rare.

09:38.730 --> 09:40.740
Hell, I'd chomp down on some raw meat!

09:41.230 --> 09:42.580
Wait...

09:51.330 --> 09:52.110
Hey, now!

09:52.110 --> 09:53.870
You greedy little sun bear!

09:54.110 --> 09:56.210
Huh? What was I just...

09:56.210 --> 09:57.490
Masa-san, that's no good!

09:57.490 --> 09:59.470
You went total bear mode just now.

09:59.470 --> 10:01.270
Wait, really? No joke?

10:01.270 --> 10:03.120
Shizuru-chan, how was your 
meeting after school?

10:03.120 --> 10:04.340
Huh? Meeting?

10:04.340 --> 10:06.740
Oh, it was totally no big deal.

10:06.740 --> 10:08.460
He asked you about your career path, right?

10:08.460 --> 10:10.340
Yeah, he asked what I wanted to do,

10:10.340 --> 10:13.200
so I said, "look for her," 
and he gave me a lecture.

10:13.980 --> 10:15.540
By "her," you mean...

10:31.550 --> 10:32.600
They're here.

10:47.890 --> 10:49.950
Sorry we're late!

10:50.710 --> 10:52.750
Taka-san, you're hogging <i>all</i> of it?!

10:52.750 --> 10:54.240
First come, first served!

10:54.250 --> 10:56.550
Nothing but meat on the brain. How childish.

10:56.550 --> 10:58.580
Looks like another bumper harvest for Agano.

10:58.580 --> 10:59.310
I'm real grateful.

10:59.310 --> 11:00.740
How was it, Neko-nii?

11:00.740 --> 11:01.860
Did you hear anything?

11:01.860 --> 11:03.960
Nope, another bust this time.

11:04.230 --> 11:05.270
Oh...

11:05.530 --> 11:06.770
What about rumors?

11:06.770 --> 11:09.290
Like new faces in town, or people leaving.

11:09.290 --> 11:10.610
Any rumors like that?

11:11.440 --> 11:14.030
Nope, none that I heard.

11:14.030 --> 11:17.000
Not many settlements are equipped 
for outside communication,

11:17.000 --> 11:20.330
so you'd expect news to bubble up 
quickly if anyone new appeared.

11:20.330 --> 11:21.010
How about you?

11:21.010 --> 11:23.240
Nothing to report here in Agano.

11:23.240 --> 11:25.320
I'm out patrolling every day, too.

11:25.320 --> 11:26.350
I see...

11:26.350 --> 11:27.440
You three.

11:27.440 --> 11:29.070
I finally found the things you asked for.

11:29.070 --> 11:29.940
Yes!

11:29.940 --> 11:31.240
My <i>NeriAli</i> mook!

11:31.240 --> 11:33.120
You know that's a secondhand copy?

11:33.120 --> 11:34.540
I'll take what I can get.

11:34.540 --> 11:37.080
It's not like they put out 
new books anymore.

11:37.080 --> 11:39.090
Wow, I'm surprised you found that.

11:39.090 --> 11:41.670
An <i>Alice in Nerima Land</i>, um...

11:40.470 --> 11:45.600
<b>Alice in Nerima Land
Official Fanbook</b>

11:41.670 --> 11:42.860
It's a mook.

11:42.860 --> 11:44.460
This takes me back!

11:44.460 --> 11:50.190
Up until the 7G incident, it aired every 
Thursday night at 12:30 on Teletama.

11:50.190 --> 11:52.250
I laughed at all the surreal poisons.

11:52.250 --> 11:54.850
Such an adorable, romantic story.

11:54.850 --> 11:56.980
Are you talking about the same show?

11:56.980 --> 11:57.520
Yeah.

11:57.520 --> 11:58.770
Hey, listen, Neko-san.

11:58.770 --> 12:00.670
Please let me work with you!

12:00.670 --> 12:02.190
Huh? Not a chance.

12:02.190 --> 12:03.460
Nothing's going to change my mind.

12:03.460 --> 12:04.600
It's too dangerous.

12:04.600 --> 12:07.370
I'm a 2-dan in Agano jiu-jitsu, you know.

12:09.060 --> 12:12.670
After the 7G incident, 
Bear was the first one to fall.

12:13.060 --> 12:16.670
Pelican, Kangaroo, and Hikyaku 
followed, one after another.

12:17.110 --> 12:20.250
We keep going because we're 
the only delivery company left,

12:20.250 --> 12:21.970
but that could change at any time.

12:23.720 --> 12:26.030
I'll make sure to tell you 
if I find out anything.

12:26.030 --> 12:27.000
So just be patient.

12:27.780 --> 12:29.510
Just like how I found that book,

12:29.510 --> 12:32.060
maybe things will just work out eventually.

12:32.060 --> 12:33.740
"Maybe"?

12:33.740 --> 12:35.570
Don't talk your way out of this!

12:37.060 --> 12:40.070
Dang it. Neko-san's a tough one.

12:39.270 --> 12:40.520
There they go.

12:40.520 --> 12:42.360
Another month of waiting...

12:42.360 --> 12:45.040
Or more, depending on how things go.

12:45.040 --> 12:45.730
Huh?

12:45.730 --> 12:47.440
Nadeko-chan, you bought something?

12:47.440 --> 12:48.360
What is it?

12:48.360 --> 12:49.450
Oh, this?

12:49.450 --> 12:51.130
It's a sweet myrtle flower shrub.

12:51.130 --> 12:52.210
Sweet what?

12:52.210 --> 12:53.110
Let me see.

12:53.110 --> 12:55.120
Why flowers?

12:55.120 --> 12:56.090
Will it even grow here?

12:56.350 --> 13:00.530
The only things that grow in Agano are rice, 
wheat or barley, and bitter melon.

13:00.530 --> 13:01.410
Yeah.

13:01.410 --> 13:04.520
But I really wanted some sweet myrtle 
for some reason.

13:04.520 --> 13:07.590
I wonder why I suddenly wanted it.

13:07.590 --> 13:08.900
What could the reason be?

13:08.900 --> 13:10.220
Don't ask us.

13:10.220 --> 13:11.260
Sweet myrtle?

13:11.630 --> 13:13.440
Huh? I think, in the past...

13:13.440 --> 13:14.980
So what'd you buy, Akira?

13:14.980 --> 13:17.380
<i>The Book of Black Magic</i> by Tatsuhiko.

13:17.380 --> 13:18.320
Tatsuhiko?

13:18.320 --> 13:21.880
The only Tatsuhiko it could be 
is Tatsuhiko Shibusawa!

13:21.880 --> 13:23.560
That's not true.

13:24.420 --> 13:25.950
What's up, Shizuru-chan?

13:25.950 --> 13:27.660
<b>March 1, 2024 (Reiwa 6)</b>

13:26.200 --> 13:28.750
There are still places 
that publish newspapers?

13:28.750 --> 13:31.290
"Diamond Gates Amplified Further," it says.

13:31.290 --> 13:32.210
What's that mean?

13:32.210 --> 13:33.800
Wait, is that...

13:33.800 --> 13:34.870
What now?

13:34.870 --> 13:35.980
Yoka-chan!

13:35.980 --> 13:37.350
Huh? No way.

13:37.350 --> 13:39.460
Yoka-chan! That's Yoka-chan!

13:39.460 --> 13:41.090
Huh? You mean <i>our</i> Yoka-chan?

13:41.090 --> 13:43.230
What other Yoka-chan could it be?

13:43.230 --> 13:44.450
Whoa, what's going on?

13:44.450 --> 13:45.480
When was this photo taken?

13:45.480 --> 13:46.390
It says last month.

13:46.390 --> 13:47.230
For real?

13:47.230 --> 13:48.510
I don't believe it!

13:48.510 --> 13:50.950
What's she doing in Ikebukuro?

13:51.950 --> 13:53.750
I need to tell Grandma Koyuki!

13:53.750 --> 13:55.200
Shizuru-chan!

13:56.710 --> 14:02.020
<i>On that day two years ago, 
the world changed entirely.</i>

14:02.020 --> 14:05.560
<i>The distance between train stations, 
and between towns,</i>

14:05.560 --> 14:07.410
<i>suddenly grew to impossible lengths.</i>

14:07.410 --> 14:08.940
<i>And it wasn't just the geography.</i>

14:08.940 --> 14:11.960
<i>All the people and living things 
completely changed.</i>

14:12.360 --> 14:16.240
<i>In Agano, all the grown-ups 
turned into animals.</i>

14:16.240 --> 14:19.930
<i>And while they can still reason like humans,</i>

14:19.930 --> 14:24.950
<i>I get the feeling that they'll 
fully turn into animals eventually.</i>

14:24.950 --> 14:28.590
<i>But it could be a lot worse 
than it is in Agano.</i>

14:27.090 --> 14:28.590
<b>Koyuki





Yoka</b>

14:27.090 --> 14:28.590
<b>Nakatomi</b>

14:29.120 --> 14:30.340
Grandma!

14:30.340 --> 14:31.430
Grandma Koyuki!

14:31.430 --> 14:32.010
Look!

14:46.840 --> 14:49.070
<i>It took everyone by surprise at first.</i>

14:49.070 --> 14:51.620
<i>Shock from being turned into weird animals,</i>

14:51.620 --> 14:54.400
<i>as well as anger and utter despair.</i>

14:54.710 --> 14:59.140
<i>A number of folks formed a survey team 
and ventured outside Agano.</i>

14:59.140 --> 15:02.260
<i>Half of them got cold feet 
and came running back.</i>

15:02.260 --> 15:04.000
<i>The other half never returned.</i>

15:04.240 --> 15:06.680
Grandma Koyuki was crying.

15:06.680 --> 15:10.010
I mean, she <i>did</i> find out that 
her only grandchild is alive.

15:10.010 --> 15:11.310
They must be tears of joy.

15:11.310 --> 15:12.530
That makes sense.

15:12.530 --> 15:14.940
Grandma Koyuki's not getting 
any younger, either.

15:14.940 --> 15:17.350
Guinea pigs die after five or six years.

15:17.350 --> 15:17.950
Huh?

15:17.950 --> 15:20.430
Why would you <i>say</i> that, Akira?

15:20.430 --> 15:22.160
<i>You</i> brought up her age, Reimi!

15:22.160 --> 15:23.960
Learn to have some sympathy!

15:23.960 --> 15:25.930
I was trying to teach you something!

15:24.150 --> 15:25.930
Play nice!

15:27.820 --> 15:29.550
Shizuru-chan!

15:30.760 --> 15:31.930
Got you!

15:39.640 --> 15:40.950
I'm home.

15:42.610 --> 15:48.210
<i>They say these phenomena were caused 
by the 7G network going haywire.</i>

15:48.210 --> 15:51.820
<i>That said, no one knows how 
to change it all back.</i>

15:51.820 --> 15:54.550
<i>Or, well, I feel like no one really wants to.</i>

15:57.560 --> 15:58.810
Welcome home.

15:58.810 --> 15:59.870
I'm back.

15:59.870 --> 16:01.550
I made dinner.

16:01.550 --> 16:03.960
I wish it wasn't just the 
usual bitter melon and rice.

16:03.960 --> 16:05.340
Make sure you heat it up first.

16:05.340 --> 16:06.800
Yeah, thanks.

16:06.800 --> 16:12.070
<i>7G is to thank, or maybe to blame, 
for the fact that we barely get electricity.</i>

16:12.600 --> 16:17.290
<i>We don't get TV or internet, 
but we can use PHS over short distances.</i>

16:17.650 --> 16:22.580
<i>The fridge works, but the breaker trips 
with both the fridge and microwave running.</i>

16:22.580 --> 16:26.840
<i>We can't use energy as much 
as we want, like we used to.</i>

16:26.840 --> 16:29.410
<i>Heck, I'm not even sure if this </i>is<i> electricity.</i>

16:29.790 --> 16:34.260
<i>It's more like an energy similar to 
electricity that runs along the rails.</i>

16:37.160 --> 16:38.920
I see now.

16:38.920 --> 16:41.030
So that's what you're like, Shizuru.

16:41.610 --> 16:42.670
Huh?

16:42.670 --> 16:44.670
What's <i>that</i> supposed to mean?

16:44.670 --> 16:46.660
I could say the same about you, Yoka!

16:46.970 --> 16:48.330
That's right.

16:48.980 --> 16:51.180
This is how I am.

16:51.830 --> 16:52.560
Sorry!

16:53.370 --> 16:54.950
What are you sorry about?!

16:54.950 --> 16:58.490
I don't care about you anymore, Yoka!

16:59.430 --> 17:01.480
What did she mean, that's what I'm like?

17:02.080 --> 17:05.280
<i>That was the last time I saw Yoka.</i>

17:05.280 --> 17:06.450
<i>We haven't met since,</i>

17:06.820 --> 17:08.460
<i>and I've had no luck searching for her.</i>

17:09.170 --> 17:12.630
No wonder I couldn't find her. 
She's in Ikebukuro!

17:12.920 --> 17:15.160
I was sure she had to be near Agano.

17:15.160 --> 17:17.840
I spent two whole years looking for her!

17:17.840 --> 17:19.130
Sheesh!

17:19.500 --> 17:20.630
Pochi-san.

17:21.610 --> 17:25.790
Pochi-san, I wonder why you didn't turn human.

17:25.790 --> 17:28.390
All the human grown-ups turn into animals,

17:28.390 --> 17:30.730
so it wouldn't be weird if you turned human.

17:31.170 --> 17:32.690
It all makes sense.

17:32.690 --> 17:36.650
If Yoka was nearby, 
you would have let me know.

17:36.650 --> 17:38.000
Since she's your owner.

17:38.460 --> 17:41.070
How come I never noticed?

17:43.960 --> 17:45.190
Good evening.

17:45.190 --> 17:46.300
Hello there.

17:51.120 --> 17:53.170
What's the matter, Zenjiro-san?

17:53.170 --> 17:55.300
It's dangerous to be on the tracks.

17:55.300 --> 17:56.340
Let's head back.

17:56.340 --> 17:59.470
C-Cap...

17:59.470 --> 18:00.090
Cap?

18:04.130 --> 18:05.120
What?

18:06.570 --> 18:08.940
Is this string from a cap?

18:08.940 --> 18:10.860
Pochi-san, do you recognize this?

18:12.830 --> 18:14.780
What? You do?

18:14.780 --> 18:15.510
Hey!

18:15.510 --> 18:17.560
Zenjiro-san, that's dangerous!

18:28.540 --> 18:30.620
Is there something inside?

18:47.240 --> 18:47.950
Yeah, yeah.

18:47.950 --> 18:49.850
Here's your choo-choo cap.

18:50.180 --> 18:52.800
That damn rotten dunghead Pontaro!

18:52.800 --> 18:55.030
How many times did I tell him 
to give up on 7G?

18:55.030 --> 18:56.860
There's no way anyone 
would adopt that standard!

18:56.860 --> 18:57.820
What?!

18:57.820 --> 19:02.270
Ignoring the many researchers who warned 
that it threatened the laws of physics!

19:02.270 --> 19:05.280
Blindly accepting only the unreliable data 
from those who sought to profit!

19:05.280 --> 19:08.380
Instead of being happy with the worst, 
why'd you have to insist on the double worst?

19:08.380 --> 19:09.680
You no-good piece of living waste!

19:09.680 --> 19:11.300
Not only did you get in my way,

19:11.300 --> 19:13.450
you even wibble-wobbled me 
with wibble-wobble surgery!

19:13.450 --> 19:15.750
You incorrigible, sly scoundrel!

19:16.040 --> 19:17.550
But just you wait!

19:17.550 --> 19:19.500
I'll make sure I put an end to 7G!

19:19.500 --> 19:21.870
I won't let you take over Ikebukuro!

19:21.870 --> 19:23.350
Wait, did you say "Ikebukuro"?

19:23.350 --> 19:24.160
I sure did.

19:24.160 --> 19:25.890
I can't leave Ikebukuro alone like this!

19:25.890 --> 19:27.170
I must stop him immediately!

19:27.170 --> 19:30.400
It looks like I, Taira Zenjiro, am left with 
no choice but to ride this 2000 series—

19:30.400 --> 19:32.200
Well, no, that's...

19:33.400 --> 19:35.760
You're Chikura Shizuru, aren't you?

19:35.760 --> 19:37.420
I once saw you get stuck in a ditch...

19:37.420 --> 19:38.320
Never mind that!

19:38.320 --> 19:40.860
More importantly, how do you 
ride this 2000 whatever?

19:40.860 --> 19:42.660
Can you drive this thing, Zenjiro-san?

19:43.470 --> 19:45.190
Can I drive this thing?

19:45.190 --> 19:45.910
Of course—

19:49.620 --> 19:50.460
What?!

19:50.460 --> 19:51.110
Wait, why?!

19:51.110 --> 19:52.370
Let's try this again!

19:53.370 --> 19:54.950
Why?!

19:54.950 --> 19:56.320
One more time!

19:56.320 --> 19:58.570
Ah, jeez!

20:00.940 --> 20:02.390
What the heck?

20:02.390 --> 20:05.520
The cap doesn't turn you back? Really?

20:05.520 --> 20:06.930
Hey, you.

20:07.620 --> 20:08.800
I see.

20:09.290 --> 20:10.930
Do your best to stay safe out there.

20:10.930 --> 20:13.140
Thanks, Mom.

20:13.140 --> 20:14.190
I'll be going.

20:14.490 --> 20:16.910
If you happen to meet an arrogant wolverine,

20:16.910 --> 20:20.440
tell him to snap out of it 
and come back home.

20:20.440 --> 20:21.400
Okay.

20:21.400 --> 20:23.080
I'll make sure I tell Dad.

20:23.390 --> 20:24.490
Hoshi Nadeshiko.

20:24.490 --> 20:25.180
Here.

20:25.180 --> 20:26.170
Kuga Reimi.

20:26.170 --> 20:26.800
Here.

20:26.800 --> 20:28.250
Shinonome Akira.

20:28.250 --> 20:28.880
Here.

20:28.880 --> 20:31.450
Nakatomi Yoka... is taking an absence.

20:31.450 --> 20:32.760
Chikura Shizuru.

20:32.760 --> 20:35.190
Shizuru's out again?

20:35.190 --> 20:37.500
None of you know what Shizuru's up to?

20:37.500 --> 20:41.890
When I ran into her two nights ago, 
she said she solved the mystery of the cap.

20:41.890 --> 20:44.770
She was running with Pochi-san 
by Agano-juku-mae.

20:44.770 --> 20:45.700
What mystery?

20:45.700 --> 20:47.760
Wait, what's she ditching class to do?

20:47.760 --> 20:48.510
Delinquency?

20:48.510 --> 20:50.220
Is Shizuru-chan turning into a delinquent?

20:50.220 --> 20:52.940
There's really no point to 
delinquent conduct out here,

20:52.940 --> 20:55.140
so there's no need to worry about that.

20:57.150 --> 20:59.740
Iguchi-sensei, thank you 
for everything you've done.

20:59.740 --> 21:00.930
I'm dropping out of school!

21:00.930 --> 21:01.900
What?!

21:03.020 --> 21:04.380
Check, check, check.

21:04.380 --> 21:06.290
Check, check, check, check.

21:06.290 --> 21:07.250
Check!

21:07.250 --> 21:10.240
I can't go with you, because reasons, 
but it looks like you'll be just fine.

21:10.240 --> 21:13.650
Go out there and see the world 
ravaged by 7G with your own eyes!

21:13.650 --> 21:15.470
I look forward to hearing back from you.

21:15.470 --> 21:18.060
And remember, the most important 
thing for survival is—

21:18.660 --> 21:21.660
Ah, right in the middle of talking again!

21:21.660 --> 21:22.950
Well, it's all good.

21:22.950 --> 21:23.880
I got the gist of it.

21:23.880 --> 21:24.950
Not good!

21:24.340 --> 21:25.420
It's not good!

21:24.810 --> 21:25.580
Not good at all!

21:25.580 --> 21:26.590
Whoa, you scared me!

21:26.590 --> 21:28.940
Don't give me that, Shizuru-chan!

21:28.940 --> 21:30.350
You're dropping out of school?

21:30.350 --> 21:31.250
Yeah.

21:31.250 --> 21:32.410
Take care of everyone.

21:32.410 --> 21:33.340
I'll be going now.

21:33.340 --> 21:34.230
Huh? Where?

21:35.310 --> 21:36.300
Ikebukuro.

21:37.320 --> 21:38.540
Wait, for real?

21:38.540 --> 21:39.640
Why all of a sudden?

21:39.640 --> 21:41.140
It's not sudden at all.

21:41.140 --> 21:42.500
I took the time to prepare.

21:46.310 --> 21:47.920
Whoa! It's leaving!

21:48.340 --> 21:49.730
Hold on. I'll go too.

21:49.730 --> 21:50.860
I'll go with you!

21:50.860 --> 21:51.570
What?!

21:51.570 --> 21:52.240
Wait!

21:52.240 --> 21:54.430
Really? Hey! No way!

22:07.300 --> 22:10.010
30 Stops Left Until Ikebukuro
